From: RTP-LLM build owners <rtp-llm@alibaba-inc.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wheelmaker: store instead of deflate, and force zip64

Two independent needs, both driven by how large RTP-LLM wheels are (multi-GB,
dominated by prebuilt .so payloads):

1. compression=ZIP_STORED instead of ZIP_DEFLATED.
   The payload is already-compiled binary; deflating it costs minutes of wheel
   build time per profile for a few percent size gain, and costs again on every
   install. Storing is the right trade for an internally distributed wheel.

2. force_zip64=True when writing each member.
   wheelmaker streams members through ZipFile.open(..., "w") without declaring
   the size upfront, so zipfile cannot decide on its own whether zip64 is
   needed and defaults to no. Individual members here exceed the 2 GiB zip64
   threshold (libtorch and friends), which fails the write without this flag.

Upstream tracking: not filed — (1) is a local distribution-policy choice
upstream should not take by default, and (2) is arguably an upstream bug worth
reporting once we are on a rules_python release whose wheelmaker still shows it.
Re-verify both hunks on any rules_python upgrade; if a newer wheelmaker gained
a compression knob and zip64 handling, drop this patch (and with it the
archive_override, since the other patch is already obsolete on 2.x).

Regression cover: the repository wheel packaging check validates filename, METADATA,
WHEEL tag and RECORD sampling, so a wheel that fails to write or writes a corrupt
member fails there.

Note: patch is generated without a/b prefixes, hence patch_strip = 0.
---
diff --git tools/wheelmaker.py tools/wheelmaker.py
index 8fa3e02d..59ac3d4d 100644
--- tools/wheelmaker.py
+++ tools/wheelmaker.py
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@ class _WhlFile(zipfile.ZipFile):
         mode,
         distribution_prefix: str,
         strip_path_prefixes=None,
-        compression=zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED,
+        compression=zipfile.ZIP_STORED,
         **kwargs,
     ):
         self._distribution_prefix = distribution_prefix
@@ -152,7 +152,7 @@ class _WhlFile(zipfile.ZipFile):
         hash = hashlib.sha256()
         size = 0
         with open(real_filename, "rb") as fsrc:
-            with self.open(zinfo, "w") as fdst:
+            with self.open(zinfo, "w", force_zip64=True) as fdst:
                 while True:
                     block = fsrc.read(2**20)
                     if not block:
